  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a noun modifier ({派生|はせい}～) or with する to indicate that something derives from something else. Common in academic, technical, and business contexts.\n\nIn linguistics, {派生語|はせいご} means \"derived word\" or \"derivative.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {派生|はせい}する: to derive, to branch off\n- {派生|はせい}{語|ご}: derived word, derivative\n- {派生|はせい}{商品|しょうひん}: derivative product, spin-off product\n- ～から{派生|はせい}する: to derive from ~",
